Cracking DevOps Interviews (1–2 Years Experience)

In the last few months, I have helped multiple engineers prepare for DevOps interviews.

One common feedback I hear is:
👉 “Interview questions are easy. But they are practical.”

So if you have 1 to 2 years experience, these are the topics you must be strong in.

I’ve collected the most asked questions from real interviews 👇

🔹 Explain your CI/CD pipeline architecture
🔹 What triggers your pipeline?
🔹 How do you handle build failures?
🔹 Difference between CI and CD?
🔹 What type of artifacts are generated in your pipeline?
🔹 How do you store credentials securely in Jenkins?
🔹 Explain Webhooks
🔹 What is Jenkins agent?
🔹 What is multibranch pipeline?
🔹 What is Blue-Green deployment?
🔹 What is Canary deployment?
🔹 What monitoring tools you used?
🔹 Explain observability?
🔹 What is Log aggregation?
🔹 What is difference between Logs, Metrics and Traces?
🔹 What is Docker image and Docker container.
🔹 How do you create Dockerfile?
🔹 How do you troubleshoot container issues?
🔹 What is Kubernetes Deployment and ReplicaSet?
🔹 How do you expose services in Kubernetes?
🔹 Difference between LoadBalancer, NodePort and ClusterIP
🔹 What is ConfigMap and Secret?
🔹 What is rolling update strategy?
🔹 Explain Horizontal Pod Autoscaling
🔹 What is AWS VPC and Subnet?
🔹 What is Security Group vs NACL?
🔹 What is IAM role?
🔹 Explain S3 lifecycle policy
🔹 What is Terraform state file?
🔹 What is drift in Terraform?
🔹 What is Ansible Playbook?
🔹 Difference between push and pull configuration?
🔹 How do you debug production issue?
🔹 Tell me about a recent outage you handled
🔹 What did you learn from it?
